   "html": "<p>Direct, indirect, and induced effects are also concentrated in more populous provinces. Within regions, the distribution of effect between direct, indirect, and induced effects is fairly consistent across provinces, suggesting that no single province is disproportionately affected by reduced household consumption expenditures (figure 3). Of note is the high percentage of Ontario’s reduction in gross output that is due to induced effects.</p>"
