   "html": "<h3 id=\"scenario-2-agriculture-agrifood-and-seafood-2\">Scenario 2: Agriculture, agrifood and seafood</h3>\n<p class=\"scenario-lead\">Exports to the US in agriculture, agrifood and seafood industries decrease by 7% to 16%.</p>\n<p>In scenario 2, both job loss and absolute decrease in value-added are highest in Ontario, but Alberta takes the second rank for decreases in value-added (though not in job loss). The other two prairie provinces, Manitoba and Saskatchewan, also show considerable absolute decreases in value-added and jobs lost.</p>\n<p>When job loss is normalized by population, the Maritime provinces join the prairie provinces with the most highly concentrated job loss (Figure G). Ontario, Quebec, and British Columbia’s job loss per 1,000 population is slightly less than that of Canada as a whole.</p>"
