   "html": "<h3 id=\"scenario-4-softwood-lumber-2\">Scenario 4: Softwood lumber</h3>\n<p class=\"scenario-lead\">Exports of softwood lumber to the US decrease by -12%.</p>\n<p>Tariffs on softwood lumber have the greatest job effects by far on British Columbia, followed by New Brunswick (Figure 10). Effects on gross output, particularly direct effects, are almost entirely concentrated in British Columbia, Quebec, Alberta and Ontario (Figure 11). Ontario’s large share of induced effects is also notable.</p>"
